// ##########################################################################
//* ############  FLAP CONTROLLER DIAGNOSTICS -- GENERATED  ##################
// ##########################################################################
//  GENERATED by apply_flap_diagnostics.py -- edit that, not this file.
//
//  What the DEVICE says about itself, as opposed to what openHAB asked for.
//  Created 2026-08-24, after flap 3 was found swinging 124 mm in 88 seconds
//  with the rod stationary while reporting Health OK -- see that script's
//  header for the evidence and `flap_fault.rules` for what is done about it.
//
//  ================  THE ONE THING TO KNOW  ================================
//  FlapActuator_N_DeviceTarget = -1 means NO STANDING TARGET.
//  It is not a position.  Test for < 0 before doing anything else with it, or
//  a page will tell an operator the flap is closed when nothing is holding it
//  anywhere at all.
//  =========================================================================
//
//  _DeviceTarget vs _Target: the first is what the controller holds, the second
//  is what the slider last sent.  They disagree when a command was lost, or when
//  a controller rebooted -- the target lives in RAM only and does not survive.
//  That disagreement is itself a fault signal; `flap_fault.rules` uses it.
//
//  _Driving is NOT persisted.  It toggles throughout a calibration and carries
//  no history worth keeping; _Mode covers the same ground for the record.
//
//  _Reachable binds the `reachable` channel, which has existed in mqtt.things
//  since the flaps were first added and had no Item until 2026-08-24.  It is the
//  LWT, so it is the ONLY authoritative answer to "is this controller on the
//  bus".  Without it, "no position" and "no controller" look identical -- and
//  they are not: flaps 12, 16 and 18 are online and answering, they simply have
//  no potentiometer fitted.

Number FlapActuator_1_DeviceTarget "Flap 1 device target [%d] mm"   (gPersist_On_Every_Change) { channel="mqtt:topic:localMQTTbroker:flap_actuator_1:device_target" }
String FlapActuator_1_Mode         "Flap 1 controller mode [%s]"   (gPersist_On_Every_Change) { channel="mqtt:topic:localMQTTbroker:flap_actuator_1:device_mode" }
Number FlapActuator_1_Driving      "Flap 1 driving [%d]"                                      { channel="mqtt:topic:localMQTTbroker:flap_actuator_1:device_driving" }
String FlapActuator_1_Health       "Flap 1 sensor health [%s]"     (gPersist_On_Every_Change) { channel="mqtt:topic:localMQTTbroker:flap_actuator_1:device_health" }
String FlapActuator_1_Reachable    "Flap 1 link [%s]"              (gPersist_On_Every_Change) { channel="mqtt:topic:localMQTTbroker:flap_actuator_1:reachable" }
String FlapActuator_1_Status       "Flap 1 status [%s]"            (gFlapStatus, gPersist_On_Every_Change)
